course: dictionary
lesson: 12649
title: Dispose of and disposed to
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To dispose of something means to get rid of it, by throwing it away or taking it somewhere else. «We dispose of our apple cores in the compost bin.» The compost bin is where the cores go to be got rid of, so dispose of means get rid of.
explain: Check the words around it for clues. «Please dispose of the broken glass carefully, so nobody gets hurt.» The word carefully and the reason after it tell you that dispose of is about getting rid of something in a safe way.
explain: Dispose has a second, more formal meaning. «She is disposed to help anyone who asks.» Disposed to means willing or likely to do something. When you see disposed to, ask yourself: does the sentence mean willing? If it does, you have found the meaning.
fact: Dispose means to get rid of something, such as throwing it away.
fact: The usual phrase is «dispose of», as in «dispose of rubbish», not «dispose rubbish».
fact: Some things must be disposed of safely, such as batteries, medicines and broken glass.
fact: «Disposal» is the noun: waste disposal means getting rid of waste.
fact: To be disposed to do something (formal) means to be willing or likely to do it.
exercise: «We dispose of our old paper in the recycling bin.» What does dispose of mean here? | Read carefully | *Get rid of | Keep forever
exercise: «Batteries must be disposed of safely, never thrown on a bonfire.» What is the safest way to dispose of old batteries? | Leave them on the floor | Put them on the bonfire | *Take them to a battery recycling point
exercise: «The new neighbour seemed disposed to be friendly.» What does disposed to mean? | Too tired to speak | Unable to move | Forced to be sad | *Willing or likely to
test: «Please dispose of the broken glass carefully.» Why must the glass be disposed of carefully? | To keep it for later | *To stop someone getting hurt | To make it shine | Because glass is fun to play with
test: Which is an example of disposing of rubbish in a way that helps the planet? | *Putting food scraps in the compost bin | Dropping litter in the park | Leaving old medicine on the table | Burning plastic in the garden
exam: Which word is the noun for getting rid of waste? | Disposing | Dispose | *Disposal | Disposed
